+To get information about the built-in rules (for example, to list them in an
+editor), the `getRules` method can be used:
+
+```javascript
+/**
+ * Gets information about the built-in rules.
+ *
+ * @returns {RuleInformation[]} Array of rule information objects.
+ */
+function getRules() { ... }
+```
+
+Each call returns a new array of plain objects (in rule order) with these
+properties, so changing the result does not affect the library:
+
+- `names` (`string[]`): Rule name(s), e.g., `["MD001", "heading-increment"]`.
+- `description` (`string`): Rule description.
+- `tags` (`string[]`): Rule tag(s).
+- `information` (`string`): URL of the rule's documentation.
+- `fixable` (`boolean`): Whether the rule can fix what it reports.
+
+```javascript
+import { getRules } from "markdownlint";
+
+// Displays the name and description of each built-in rule
+for (const rule of getRules()) {
+  console.log(`${rule.names.join("/")}: ${rule.description}`);
+}
+```
+
 [semver]: https://semver.org

